      "latency_ms": 2330.6,
      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 565,
      "output": "At its most fundamental level, **water** is a chemical compound made up of two types of atoms: **hydrogen** and **oxygen**. Its chemical formula is **$H_2O$**—meaning every single molecule of water is composed of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.\n\nHowever, to humans, Earth, and all known life, water is much more than a simple chemical formula. Here is a breakdown of what water is through different lenses:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Physical Substance\nWater is a transparent, odorless, and tasteless liquid at standard temperature and pressure. It is unique because it is the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in **three physical states**:\n*   **Liquid:** Oceans, rivers, rain.\n*   **Solid (Ice):** Glaciers, snow, ice cubes.\n*   **Gas (Vapor):** Steam, humidity, clouds.\n\n### 2. \"The Universal Solvent\"\nWater has a unique molecular structure. Because the oxygen atom pulls harder on the shared electrons than the hydrogen atoms do, water is a **polar molecule** (one side has a slight negative charge, and the other has a slight positive charge). \n\nThis polarity allows water to dissolve more substances than any other liquid. It is why salt and sugar dissolve in water, and it is how water transports vital nutrients and minerals through the bloodstream of animals and the vascular systems of plants.\n\n### 3. The Elixir of Life\nAs far as science knows, **life cannot exist without water.** \n*   **Biological Medium:** The human body is made up of about 60% water. It regulates body temperature, lubricates joints, flushes out waste, and provides the moist environment necessary for cellular chemical reactions.\n*   **Habitat:** It provides a home for millions of aquatic species, from microscopic plankton to blue whales.\n\n### 4. Earth’s Driving Force\nOften called the \"Blue Planet,\" Earth’s surface is about **71% water**, with the vast majority (about 96.5%) contained in the oceans as saltwater. \n*   **The Water Cycle:** Water continuously moves through the Earth system via evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection, driving global weather patterns and climates.\n*   **Temperature Regulation:** Water has a very high \"heat capacity,\" meaning it can absorb and release large amounts of heat. This helps regulate the temperature of the entire planet, preventing extreme global temperature swings.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\nWater is the lifeblood of our planet. It shapes our geography, regulates our climate, drives our weather, and makes up the majority of living things. Without it, life as we know it would simply cease to exist."
